     "value": "stair_of_hooks"
    }
   ],
   "narration": "'The Ember goes home to Harrow's Rest,' you say, and Sera nods once, sharp, like she's nailing it to the air between you. 'One promise, heard,' she says, and starts down the stair ahead of you, lantern light swinging over hook-scarred stone. You're three steps down when a voice unfolds from the shadows below \u2014 unhurried, amused. 'Travellers,' Moss says, stepping into the light with his hands open and empty. 'I don't suppose you'd sell before you've even opened the door.'",
