  {
   "turn": 3,
   "action": "I hear Moss out \u2014 what exactly is he offering for the Ember?",
   "deltas": [],
   "narration": "Moss spreads his hands wider, a showman's gesture. 'Silver \u2014 good weight of it, enough to see Harrow's Rest through more than one winter, if that's what you're carrying home. I don't ask how you open that door, and I don't touch it myself. I ask after, on your way back down, when it's warm in your hands.' He glances at Sera, then back to you, patient as stone. 'That's the whole of the offer. No tricks folded into it.'",
