   "narration": "The stair narrows into the vault floor, cold air pressing close, and the great door stands before you scarred with old locks \u2014 unopened still, waiting on the key in your fist. Sera doesn't look at you as she says it: 'Moss's silver. You shook on it right in front of me.' She counts it off like she counts oil, flat and sure. 'That's one promise to me, one to him, and only one Ember between them. I'll be watching which hand you open first.' She sets her lantern down and waits, arms crossed, eyes on the door.",
