   "narration": "Two steps up the hooks and the lantern gutters to nothing \u2014 the last of the oil spent, the flame folding into a thin red thread and then dark. You don't need light to find Moss, though; he's already there, exactly where the stair narrows, silver pouch weighing his palm like he's been waiting since you passed the first time. 'There you are,' he says, easy as ever, no edge in it. 'You said the Ember for my silver. I've kept my word on my end \u2014 every coin's here. So.' He doesn't reach for it. He just holds his hand out, patient, and waits for you to be the one who decides what a promise is worth.",
